    Block {
      BlockType		      SubSystem
      Name		      "Draw_End_Circle"
      SID		      "499"
      Ports		      [2, 1]
      Position		      [2005, 2441, 2225, 2494]
      ZOrder		      336
      BackgroundColor	      "green"
      AncestorBlock	      "Video/Show_Target_With_Label"
      LibraryVersion	      "*1.938"
      MinAlgLoopOccurrences   off
      PropExecContextOutsideSubsystem off
      RTWSystemCode	      "Auto"
      FunctionWithSeparateData off
      Opaque		      off
      RequestExecContextInheritance off
      MaskHideContents	      off
      Object {
	$PropName		"MaskObject"
	$ObjectID		20
	$ClassName		"Simulink.Mask"
	Type			"Show_Target_With_Label"
	Description		"This block returns a VCODE that, when sent to the Process_Video_CMD block, will cause a single target w"
	"ith a text label to be drawn. The label will be centered at the centroid of the target. Target parameters are specifi"
	"ed in the Target Table according to the columns defined below and the row input to this block.\n"
	Help			"Used to draw a single, stationary target with a label.\n\n<H2>Library </H2>\nVideo\n\n<H2>Description </H2>\n"
	"This block returns a VCODE, which when sent to the Process_Video_CMD block will draw a single stationary target with "
	"a label. The VCODE contains all of the target parameters necessary to draw the target and the label.\n<P>\nThe VCODE "
	"is generated from information contained in the Target Table. Which parts of the Target Table are used is determined b"
	"y the columns selected (see Parameters and Dialog Box below).<P>\n\n<p>For example, assume the \"row\" input is 2, th"
	"e \"type of target\" is set to \"rectangle\" and the \"Target Table Columns\" is set to [3 0 0 4 5 0 6 7 4]. \nThen u"
	"sing the sample target table below a red rectangle will be drawn at (20cm, 40cm) with a width of 10cm and a height of"
	" 3cm. \nThe rectangle will have the word \"Maybe\" in yellow on it in letters 3cm heigh. The zeros in the  \"Target T"
	"able Columns\" indicate those parameters are not used (i.e. no stroke color, no stroke width, and no rotation).\n\n<p"
	"><tt>\n______________________________________________________________________<br>\n|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb"
	"sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;| X Pos | Y pos |&nbsp;&nbsp;Fill | Width | Height |&nbsp;&nbsp;Text | TColor |<br>\n-----"
	"-----------------------------------------------------------------<br>\n| target 1 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;10 |&nbsp;"
	"&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;10 | white |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nb"
	"sp;Yes |&nbsp;&nbsp;green |<br>\n| target 2 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;20 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;40 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs"
	"p;red |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;10 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3 | Maybe | yellow |<br>\n| target 3 |&nbsp;&n"
	"bsp;&nbsp;-40 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;10 |&nbsp;&nbsp;blue |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3 |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp"
	";&nbsp;&nbsp;4 | Wrong |&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;red |\n--------------------------------------------------------------"
	"--------<br>\n\n\n</tt>\n\n\n<p>Inputs:<br>\n<B> Target_Row: </B> this scalar input determines which row in the Targe"
	"t Table is used to define the target parameters. Typically the Target_Row comes from the Trial_Protocol.  <P>\n<B> Ta"
	"rget_State: </B> this scalar input determines which state the target is in. Different states reference different colu"
	"mns in the Target Table (as defined in the Dialog Box). Typically the Target_State input is controlled by the Statefl"
	"ow chart to dynamically change the appearance of the target depending on system and/or subject behavior. Target_State"
	"=0 is a valid input, which turns the target off. The intended method for turning a target off is to set Target_State="
	"0. <BR>\n<P>\n<B>Opacity:</B> This input is only available if Source for Opacity is selected as port, in which case t"
	"he opacity for all of the targets created by this block is specified as a percentage.\nThe length of this input must "
	"either match the length of the Target_Row(s) input (i.e. which case each Opacity maps to the appropriate Target_row) "
	"\nor this input must be a scalar (in which case the Opacity maps to all of the Target_Rows).<BR>\n<P>\nThere is one o"
	"utput from this block: \n<P>\n<B> VCODE: </B> this output is a vector containing one VCODE. This output must go to th"
	"e Process_Video_CMD block of the video library for the target to actually be shown (if any other visual targets are t"
	"o be displayed, then this VCODE output must be concatenated with the other VCODES prior to connection to the Process_"
	"Video_CMD block - see Help for the Process_Video_CMD block for more information).\n<P>\nTo show multiple targets simu"
	"ltaneously, multiple copies of the Show_Target and Show_Target_With_Label blocks can be used in a Task Program. The o"
	"utput VCODES from multiple Show_Target and Show_Target_With_Label blocks must be concatenated prior to connection to "
	"the Process_Video_CMD block.\n<P>\n\n<H2>Parameters and Dialog Box</H2>\n<B>Type of Target:</B> Choose the type of ta"
	"rget specified in the target table. \n<P>\n<B>Number of Target States:</B> Choose the number of target states specifi"
	"ed in each target row. Up to five target states are allowed per target row.\n<P>\n<B>State [n] Target Table Columns:<"
	"/B> Enter the column indices that specify the relevant target attributes in the Target Table. All target types have t"
	"he same first three target attributes (fill colour, stroke colour and stroke width) and the same last three target at"
	"tributes (label text, label colour, and label height).\n<Blockquote>\n<P>\nElement 1 (fill colour) - points to the co"
	"lumn index in the Target Table containing the fill colour. If this index is 0, then the fill colour is transparent an"
	"d the Target Table is not referenced. For line targets, the fill colour is not used.\n<P>\nElement 2 (stroke colour) "
	"- points to the column index in the Target Table containing the stroke colour. If this index is 0, then the stroke co"
	"lour is transparent and the Target Table is not referenced. It is possible to use the same column index for both fill"
	" colour and stroke colour (i.e.  if single-colour targets are desired). For line targets, stroke colour defines the c"
	"olour of the line.\n<P>\nElement 3 (stroke width) - points to the column index in the Target Table containing the str"
	"oke width (cm). If no stroke is desired, then setting the stroke column index to 0 will produce a stroke width of 0  "
	"and the Target Table is not referenced.  Setting stroke column index to a value less than 0 will produce a standard 1"
	" mm stroke width, again without referencing the Target Table. For line targets, stroke width defines the width of the"
	" line.\n<P>\n<B><I>Circle</I></B> <P>\nElement 4 (radius) - radius of the circle (cm).\n<P>\n<B><I>Ellipse</I></B> <P"
	">\nElements 4-6 (ellipse properties) - major radius (cm), minor radius (cm), rotation angle (degrees). If no rotation"
	" is desired, then setting rotation column index to 0 will produce a default rotation of 0 and the Target Table will n"
	"ot be referenced.\n<P>\n<B><I>Rectangle</I></B><P>\nElements 4-6 (rectangle properties) - length (cm), height (cm), r"
	"otation angle (degrees). If no rotation is desired, then setting rotation column index to 0 will produce a default ro"
	"tation of 0 and the Target Table will not be referenced.\n<P>\n<B><I>Line</I></B><P>\nElements 4-5 (line properties) "
	"- end point x-axis position relative to start point (cm), end point y-axis position relative to start point (cm). The"
	" width and colour of the line are defined by the stroke width and the stroke colour, respectively. The fill colour co"
	"lumn is ignored (i.e. any value can be used for column 1)\n<P>\n<B><I>Triangle</I></B><P>\nElements 4-7 (triangle pro"
	"perties) - length (cm), height (cm), offset of peak of triangle relative to midpoint of the length (cm), rotation ang"
	"le (degrees). If a height column index of 0 is specified, then an equilateral triangle with sides of the specified le"
	"ngth will be created and the Target Table will not be referenced for height or peak offset. If no rotation is desired"
	", then setting a rotation column index of 0 will produce a default rotation of 0 and the Target Table will not be ref"
	"erenced.\n<P>\n<B><I>Label</I></B>\n<P>\nThe last three elements of the target state vector define the label. In orde"
	"r, these elements are:\n<P>\nLabel text - the index of the column in the Target Table containing the text used for th"
	"e label (up to 50 characters).\n<P>\nLabel colour - the index of the column in the Target Table containing the label "
	"colour. If this index is 0, then the label colour is transparent and the Target Table is not referenced.\n<P>\nLabel "
	"height - the index of the column in the Target Table containing the label height (cm).\n</Blockquote>\n<P>\nEach targ"
	"et state requires its own set of column index definitions (although multiple states can point to the same column inde"
	"x if desired).<P>\n\n<B>Source for Opacity:</B> Choose either dialog, to specify the opacity in this dialog, or port,"
	" which will create a new input to allow dynamic control of opacity. \n<P>\n<B>Opacity:</B> This parameter is only ava"
	"ilable if Source for Opacity is selected as dialog, in which case the opacity for all of the targets created by this "
	"block is specified as a percentage.\n<P>\n<B>Target Display:</B> This option determines whether the target(s) are sho"
	"wn on the operator display only, the subject display only, or both displays. \n<P>\n\n<H2>Examples</H2>\n\n<B>Example"
	" 1:</B>  Suppose a target row will be used to define 1 state for an ellipse type target. It will be an outline of an "
	"ellipse with a label in the center (using a stroke colour and a standard 1mm stroke width). The related Target Table "
	"columns are:\n<P>\ncolumn 4 = colour<BR>\ncolumn 5 = major radius<BR>\ncolumn 6 = minor radius<BR>\ncolumn 7 = orient"
	"ation<BR>\ncolumn 8 = label text<BR>\ncolumn 9 = label colour<BR>\ncolumn 10 = label height\n<P>For this example, \"S"
	"tate 1 Target Table Columns\" would equal [0 4 -1 5 6 7 8 9 10].\n<P> \n\n<H2>Related Blocks </H2>\nShow_Target<BR>\n"
	"Process_Video_CMD"
	Initialization		"block_path = gcb;  % store block path, as gcb may change with block operations\n\n%%% Get the model'"
	"s workspace, because it is required to evaluate constants from the Parameter Table Def'n block\nmodelName=bdroot(bloc"
	"k_path);\nmodelWorkspace = get_param(modelName, 'ModelWorkspace');\n\n%%% Handle background colours if link status ch"
	"anges.  \ncheckBackgroundColour(block_path, 'Video');\n\n%%% create the names of the input and output ports to displa"
	"y on the mask\noutput_block=char(find_system(block_path,'LookUnderMasks','all','FollowLinks','on','SearchDepth',1,'Bl"
	"ockType','Outport'));\noutputname=get_param(output_block,'Name');\n\ninput_block=find_system(block_path,'LookUnderMas"
	"ks','all','FollowLinks','on','SearchDepth',1,'BlockType','Inport');\ninputname1=get_param(char(input_block{1}),'Name'"
	");\ninputname2=get_param(char(input_block{2}),'Name');\nif length(input_block) >= 3\n    inputname3=get_param(char(in"
	"put_block{3}),'Name');\nend\n\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n%%% Create or replace t"
	"he opacity input port\n% Note: in earlier versions of MATLAB, the replace_block function did not work properly. When "
	"we drop support for R2007b,\n% Check to see if it works properly in R2010a and if so, then this code can be simplifie"
	"d with the use of the replace_block function\nsourceStr=get_param(block_path,'source');\n\nif strmatch(sourceStr, 'di"
	"alog')\n	if length(input_block) == 3\n		pos=get_param([block_path '/Opacity'],'position');\n		delete_line(block_path,"
	" 'Opacity/1', 'Embedded MATLAB Function/4');\n		delete_block(input_block{3});\n        add_block('built-in/Constant',"
	"[block_path '/Opacity'],'Name','Opacity');\n		set_param([block_path '/Opacity'],'position',pos);\n		add_line(block_pa"
	"th, 'Opacity/1', 'Embedded MATLAB Function/4');\n		set_param([block_path '/Opacity'],'Value','opacity');\n	end\n	disp"
	"laytext = ['disp(columntext); port_label(''output'',1,outputname); port_label(''input'',1, inputname1); port_label(''"
	"input'',2, inputname2);'];\nelse\n	if length(input_block) == 2\n		pos=get_param([block_path '/Opacity'],'position');\n"
	"		delete_line(block_path, 'Opacity/1', 'Embedded MATLAB Function/4');\n		delete_block([block_path, '/Opacity']);\n		a"
	"dd_block('built-in/Inport',[block_path '/In2'],'Name','Opacity');\n		set_param([block_path '/Opacity'],'position',pos"
	");\n		add_line(block_path, 'Opacity/1', 'Embedded MATLAB Function/4');\n 	end\n	inputname3='Opacity';\n	displaytext ="
	" ['disp(columntext); port_label(''output'',1,outputname); port_label(''input'',1, inputname1); port_label(''input'',2"
	", inputname2); port_label(''input'',3, inputname3);'];\nend\nset_param(block_path,'MaskDisplay',displaytext);\n\n\n%%"
	"%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%\n%%% Check and format the input strings for the vectors o"
	"f column entires\ntargetTypeStr=get_param(block_path, 'target_type');\n\nswitch targetTypeStr(1:3)\n	case 'Cir',		num"
	"Col = 7;\n	case 'Ell',		numCol = 9;\n    case 'Rec',		numCol = 9;\n    case 'Lin',		numCol = 8;\n    case 'Tri',		num"
	"Col = 10;\n	otherwise,		numCol = 7;\nend\n\n% % % numCol=str2num( get_param(block_path, 'num_col') );\nfor ii = 1:5\n"
	"	variableName = ['attribcol' num2str(ii)];\n	attribcoltext = get_param(block_path, variableName);\n	attribcoltext = c"
	"heckUserInputVectorLength(attribcoltext, numCol);\n	set_param(block_path, variableName, attribcoltext);\nend\n\n% the"
	" input to the Embedded MATLAB script under the mask needs to have a certain size. This creates 'padding' to add to th"
	"e \n% attribcol vectors to get to that size\nzeros_5x7_matrix = zeros(5,7);\nset_param(block_path, 'stateindices_padd"
	"ing', mat2str(zeros_5x7_matrix(:, 1:(11-numCol))) );\n\n\n%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%"
	"%%\n%%% Create the text to show on the mask\nnumStates = str2num(get_param(block_path, 'num_states'));\n\nfor ii = 1:"
	"numStates\n	variableName = ['attribcol' num2str(ii)];\n	attribcolString = get_param(block_path, variableName);\n	if i"
	"sempty(modelWorkspace)\n		% if the block is part of a library, then modelWorkspace will be empty and the other code t"
	"o evaluate attribcolStringEval will fail\n		attribcolStringEval = '[4 0 3 0 0 0 0]';\n	else\n		[attribcolValue, error"
	"Message] = BKINevalin(modelWorkspace, attribcolString);\n		attribcolStringEval = ['          ' mat2str( attribcolValu"
	"e )];\n	end\n	if ii > 1\n		columntext = strvcat(columntext, attribcolStringEval);\n	else\n		columntext = attribcolStr"
	"ingEval;\n	end\nend\n\n% Add formatting spaces so that the mask looks nice\nspace = repmat(' ', 1, round(length(colum"
	"ntext)/2));\ncolumntext=strvcat([space '(columns)'], columntext);\n\n\n"
	SelfModifiable		"on"
	Display			"disp(columntext); port_label('output',1,outputname); port_label('input',1, inputname1); port_label('input'"
	",2, inputname2);"
	IconUnits		"normalized"
	Array {
	  Type			  "Simulink.MaskParameter"
	  Dimension		  11
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    21
	    Type		    "popup"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Cell"
	      Dimension		      5
	      Cell		      "Circle"
	      Cell		      "Ellipse"
	      Cell		      "Rectangle"
	      Cell		      "Line"
	      Cell		      "Triangle"
	      PropName		      "TypeOptions"
	    }
	    Name		    "target_type"
	    Prompt		    "Type of Target"
	    Value		    "Circle"
	    Callback		    "\n%%%%\n% Because of bugs iN R2007, R2010a and R2013a (which have been reported to Mathworks), the"
	    " following code \n% is required here because in the Initialization Section it will ONLY correctly update those Ma"
	    "sk Parameters that are hidden\n% when the OK button is clicked (NOTE: the initialization code will correctly upda"
	    "te all Mask Parameters when the Apply button \n% is clicked, the bug is that it should also update everything whe"
	    "n the OK button is clicked in the absence of an Apply click)\n%\n% Adding a set_param call which updates one of t"
	    "he mask parameters will call the initialization code to run, which \"avoids\"\n% this bug. This code should be re"
	    "moved once Mathworks has fixed this bug.\n\ntemp = get_param(gcb, 'target_type');\nset_param(gcb, 'target_type', "
	    "temp);\n"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    22
	    Type		    "popup"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Cell"
	      Dimension		      5
	      Cell		      "1"
	      Cell		      "2"
	      Cell		      "3"
	      Cell		      "4"
	      Cell		      "5"
	      PropName		      "TypeOptions"
	    }
	    Name		    "num_states"
	    Prompt		    "Number of Target States"
	    Value		    "1"
	    Callback		    "block_path=gcb;\nnum_states=str2num(get_param(block_path, 'num_states'));\nvis=get_param(block_pat"
	    "h,'MaskVisibilities');\n\n%If the number of states>1, then output an array instead of a vector.\n%Only show those"
	    " inputs necessary on the Mask\noutput_block=char(find_system(block_path,'LookUnderMasks','all','SearchDepth',1,'B"
	    "lockType','Outport'));\nif num_states==1			%output of HandInTarget block is a vector\n	vis{4}='off';\n	vis{5}='of"
	    "f';\n	vis{6}='off';\n	vis{7}='off';\nelseif num_states==2					%output of HandInTarget block is an array\n	vis{4}="
	    "'on';\n	vis{5}='off';\n	vis{6}='off';\n	vis{7}='off';\nelseif num_states==3					%output of HandInTarget block is "
	    "an array\n	vis{4}='on';\n	vis{5}='on';\n	vis{6}='off';\n	vis{7}='off';\nelseif num_states==4					%output of HandI"
	    "nTarget block is an array\n	vis{4}='on';\n	vis{5}='on';\n	vis{6}='on';\n	vis{7}='off';\nelse								%output of Ha"
	    "ndInTarget block is an array\n	vis{4}='on';\n	vis{5}='on';\n	vis{6}='on';\n	vis{7}='on';\nend\nset_param(block_pa"
	    "th,'MaskVisibilities',vis);\n"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    23
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "attribcol1"
	    Prompt		    "State 1 Target Table Column(s)"
