	Block {
	  BlockType		  SubSystem
	  Name			  "KINARM_EP_Position_Controller"
	  SID			  "176"
	  Ports			  [2, 1]
	  Position		  [570, 54, 710, 101]
	  ZOrder		  2
	  BackgroundColor	  "green"
	  AncestorBlock		  "KINARM_EP_loads/KINARM_EP_Position_Controller"
	  LibraryVersion	  "*1.120"
	  MinAlgLoopOccurrences	  off
	  PropExecContextOutsideSubsystem off
	  RTWSystemCode		  "Auto"
	  FunctionWithSeparateData off
	  Opaque		  off
	  RequestExecContextInheritance	off
	  MaskHideContents	  off
	  Object {
	    $PropName		    "MaskObject"
	    $ObjectID		    68
	    $ClassName		    "Simulink.Mask"
	    Type		    "KINARM_EP_Position_Controller"
	    Description		    "<P>The KINARM_EP_Position_Controller block creates loads on the KINARM End-Point robot that imp"
	    "lement position control of the hand using a feedforward model and feedback control.\n<P>\nThe optional feedforwar"
	    "d model uses estimates of KINARM End-Point robot inertia to create an estimate of required forces. A PD feedback "
	    "controller is added to ensure optimal control.  The \"Standard Movement\" controller performance setting is optim"
	    "ized for reaching movements.  The \"Step Response\" setting is optimized for fast movements.\n<P>\nDesired positi"
	    "on input is the (x, y) end-point position (i.e. handle).\n<P>\n<b>NOTE: it is critical to set the timebase of the"
	    " desired position input signal correctly. Failure to do so will lead to robot instability, possibly damaging the "
	    "KINARM robot and/or leading to subject injury.</b>\n"
	    Help		    "Used to create loads for position control at the hand (i.e. finger-tip).\n\n<H2>Library </H2>\nKINARM_"
	    "EP_loads (sub-library of Dexterit-E)\n\n\n<H2>Description </H2>\nThe KINARM_EP_Position_Controller block creates "
	    "loads on the KINARM End-Point robot that implement position control of the hand using a feedforward model and fee"
	    "dback control.\n\nThe optional feedforward model uses estimates of KINARM End-Point robot inertia to create an es"
	    "timate of required forces. A PD feedback controller is added to ensure optimal control.  The \"Standard Movement\""
	    " controller performance setting is optimized for reaching movements.  The \"Step Response\" setting is optimized "
	    "for fast movements.\n<P>\n<B>desired_xy_position: </B> this vector input is the desired position (i.e. attractor "
	    "point) that the position controller acts on.  It should either be a [1x2] vector input or a VCODE.\nThe expected "
	    "coordinate system and units for this input are the global coordinate system and meters.\n<P>\n<B>e_reset: </B> th"
	    "is scalar input resets the velocity and acceleration to zero for the feed-forward portion of the position control"
	    "ler model when e_reset transitions from 0 to 1.  This input should be used whenever the desired_xy_position input"
	    " is being reset to a different position.  \n<P>\n<B>inertia_option: </B> this optional scalar input defines which"
	    " inertias to include for the feed-forward model.  Valid values are defined below.\n<P>\n<B>Forces: </B> this vect"
	    "or output is in a global Cartesian coordinate space as per all other KINARM End-Point load blocks.  It must be wi"
	    "red to the KINARM_EP_Apply_Loads block to actually apply the loads to the KINARM End-Point Robot.  This output ma"
	    "y be added to other Force outputs from other KINARM End-Point load blocks to create a composite load.\n<P>\n\n<H2"
	    ">Parameters and Dialog Box</H2>\n<P>\n<B>Position control on dominant arm:</B> indicates whether or not this posi"
	    "tion control is applied to the dominant arm (checked box) or non-dominant arm (unchecked box).\n<P>\n<B>Inertias "
	    "to include for feed-forward control: </B> <BR>\nChoices are: <BR>\n(port)<BR>\n0 - None <BR>\n1 - KINARM End-Poin"
	    "t robot  <BR>\n<P>\nIf the (port) option is chosen, then an inport will be created allowing dynamic control of th"
	    "e inertia options.  \nThe value wired to the inport will be mapped to the inertial choise using the values specif"
	    "ied here (i.e. appropriate values are from 0-1).\nOtherwise the option chosen will determine which inertias are i"
	    "ncluded for the feed-forward control.  \n<P>\n<B>Controller Performance: </B> <BR>\nChoices are: <BR>\n1 - Standa"
	    "rd Movement <BR>\n2 - Step Response  <BR>\n<P>\nThe \"Standard Movement\" option is optimized for movements simil"
	    "ar to normal reaching movements and provides high stiffness, but is underdamped.  \nThere can be large overshoot "
	    "following high accelerations/decellerations.\n<P>\nThe \"Step Response\" option is optimized to minimize overshoo"
	    "t to less than ~10% for step responses, but at the cost of a reduction in controller stiffness. \n<P> \nNOTE: cho"
	    "ice of Controller Performance option does not affect systems with secondary encoders - they are optimized for bot"
	    "h conditions, providing higher stiffness and reasonable damping.\nThe controller for systems with secondary encod"
	    "ers provides less than ~10% overshoot for step responses.\n<P>\n\n<B>Time base of desired position input signal ("
	    "-1 for inherited from sample time):</B> <BR>\nDefines the time base used to calculate velocity and acceleration f"
	    "rom the desired position input signal (-1 will inherit the time base from the sample time of the desired position"
	    " input signal).\nIt is critical that this time base is set correctly.\nThe time base MUST be set to the time base"
	    " used to create the desired input signal, WHICH MAY NOT BE THE SAME as the sample time of the desired input signa"
	    "l.  \n<B>Failure to set this time base correctly will lead to robot instability, possibly damaging the KINARM rob"
	    "ot and/or leading to subject injury. </B>\n<BR>\n<I>Note: to determine the sample time of a signal, first update "
	    "the model, then either select View --> Sample Time Legend or press Cntl + J.</I>\n<P>\nFor example, a Stateflow c"
	    "hart that creates a desired position signal will, by default, use the model's sample time (e.g. 0.0005 s).  \nHow"
	    "ever, that Stateflow chart may use a time base that can be any multiple of the sample time (e.g. 0.001 s, 0.005 s"
	    ", etc).  \nIf a Stateflow chart was updating the desired position every 0.001 seconds, but the output sample time"
	    " was 0.0005, then the position signal over time will look like: \n<P> \n[... x0, x0, x1, x1, x2, x2, x3, x3 ...]."
	    "\n<P>\nA velocity calculated using 0.0005 time base will be:\n<P>\n[... 0, x1-x0, 0, x2-x1, 0, x3-x2, 0 ...] / 0."
	    "0005 \n<P>\n(i.e. velocity will be 0 every other sample). \nWhereas the true velocity in this example should be c"
	    "alculated using a 0.001 time base to create:\n<P>\n [... x1-x0, x2-x1, x3-x2, ...] / 0.001.\n\n<H2>Related Blocks"
	    " </H2>\nKINARM_EP_Apply_Loads, Virtual_Trajectory"
	    Initialization	    "block_path = gcb;  % store block path, as gcb may change with block operations\n\n%%% Handle "
	    "background colours if link status changes.  \ncheckBackgroundColour(block_path, 'KINARM_EP_loads');\n\n% Handle t"
	    "he inertias_for_FF setting: swap the 'inertia_option' inport with a constant block or \n% vice versa, if necessar"
	    "y, so that it matches the setting.\nblock_type = get_param([block_path '/inertia_option'], 'BlockType');\n\nif (i"
	    "nertias_for_FF == 1) && ~strcmp(block_type, 'Inport') || ...  % if a change is required...\n   (inertias_for_FF >"
	    " 1) && strcmp(block_type, 'Inport')\n    \n    % ...delete the existing block, ...\n    pos = get_param([block_pa"
	    "th '/inertia_option'], 'Position');\n    delete_line(block_path, 'inertia_option/1', 'FF_FB_Position_Controller/7"
	    "');\n    delete_block([block_path '/inertia_option']);\n    \n    % ...add an Inport or a 0-value Constant in pla"
	    "ce of the previous block (according to\n    % the new setting), update the signal width flag, and then...\n    if"
	    " (inertias_for_FF == 1) && ~strcmp(block_type, 'Inport')\n        add_block('built-in/Inport', [block_path '/iner"
	    "tia_option']);\n     else\n        add_block('built-in/Constant', [block_path '/inertia_option']);\n        set_p"
	    "aram([block_path '/inertia_option'], 'Value', 'inertias_for_FF - 2');\n    end\n    \n    % ...connect the new bl"
	    "ock.\n    set_param([block_path '/inertia_option'], 'Position', pos);\n    add_line(block_path, 'inertia_option/1"
	    "', 'FF_FB_Position_Controller/7');\nend\n\n\n\n% Set the sample rate of the desired_position input port based on "
	    "the \n% sample rate from the mask\ninports = find_system(block_path, 'LookUnderMasks', 'all', 'FollowLinks', 'on'"
	    ", 'SearchDepth', 1, 'BlockType', 'Inport');\nset_param(inports{1}, 'SampleTime', get_param(gcb, 'sample_time') );"
	    "\n\n% Ensure the inports appear in a fixed order, and for each inport found add\n% to the list of drawing command"
	    "s a command to label it.\nfor i = 1:length(inports)\n    inport_name = char(get_param(inports(i), 'Name'));\n    "
	    "\n    if strcmp(inport_name, 'inertia_option')\n        port = '3';\n	elseif strcmp(inport_name, 'desired_positio"
	    "n')\n        port = '1';\n 	else\n		port = '2';\n		% do nothing\n	end\n    \n    set_param([block_path '/' inport"
	    "_name], 'Port', port);\nend\n"
	    SelfModifiable	    "on"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Simulink.MaskParameter"
	      Dimension		      4
	      Object {
		$ObjectID		69
		Type			"checkbox"
		Name			"use_dom_hand"
		Prompt			"Position control on dominant arm"
		Value			"on"
	      }
	      Object {
		$ObjectID		70
		Type			"popup"
		Array {
		  Type			  "Cell"
		  Dimension		  3
		  Cell			  "(port)"
		  Cell			  "None"
		  Cell			  "KINARM End Point robot"
		  PropName		  "TypeOptions"
		}
		Name			"inertias_for_FF"
		Prompt			"Inertias to include for feed-forward control: "
		Value			"KINARM End Point robot"
	      }
	      Object {
		$ObjectID		71
		Type			"popup"
		Array {
		  Type			  "Cell"
		  Dimension		  2
		  Cell			  "Standard Movement"
		  Cell			  "Step Response"
		  PropName		  "TypeOptions"
		}
		Name			"gain_choice"
		Prompt			"Controller Performance"
		Value			"Standard Movement"
	      }
	      Object {
		$ObjectID		72
		Type			"edit"
		Name			"sample_time"
		Prompt			"Time base of desired position input signal (-1 for inherited):"
		Value			"0.001"
		Callback		"%ensure that sample time parameter is valid\nsample_time_param = str2num( get_param(gcb, 'sample_time') )"
		";\nmodel_step_size = str2num(get_param(bdroot, 'FixedStep'));\n\n%default value:\nsample_time = -1;\n\n% if paramete"
		"r value is numeric, sample_time_param will not be empty\nif ~isempty(sample_time_param)\n% 	round the sample time to"
		" an integer multiple of model step size, if possible\n	if ~isempty(model_step_size) && (model_step_size > 0)\n		samp"
		"le_time = round( sample_time_param / model_step_size ) * model_step_size;\n	else\n		sample_time = sample_time_param;"
		"\n	end\n	\n	% if input value is <=0, set it = -1 (inherited)\n	if (sample_time <= 0)\n		sample_time = -1;\n	end\nend"
		"\n\nset_param(gcb, 'sample_time', num2str(sample_time) );"
	      }
	      PropName		      "Parameters"
	    }
	  }
